-Each project gets its own library, a separate database on one Postgres server, created the first time the project is opened, with its tables set up automatically. Storytree can list the projects on the server, and nothing written in one project can ever show up in another.
+Each project gets its own library, a separate database on one Postgres server, created the first time the project is opened, with its tables set up automatically, and brought up to date by the next open after storytree adds to them. Opening a project whose tables are already current touches no table, so an account let only read, or write a few kinds of record, can open it too. Storytree can list the projects on the server, and nothing written in one project can ever show up in another.

